      "writtenOn": "2022-09-22T01:18:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, in that case, what you need is actually an iterator that can return slice by slice, instead of a function that returns a single slice.\n\nSo `extract_*` can factor out the iterating logic to be simpler:\n```\npub fn extract_service_data(bytes: \u0026[u8]) -\u003e HashMap\u003cString, Vec\u003cu8\u003e\u003e {\n    let mut service_data: HashMap\u003cString, Vec\u003cu8\u003e\u003e \u003d HashMap::new();\n\n    for slice in iterate_adv_data(bytes, SERVICE_DATA_128_BIT_UUID) {\n        match Uuid::try_from(slice[0..16].to_vec()) {\n            Ok(uuid) \u003d\u003e {\n                let data \u003d slice[16..].to_vec();\n                service_data.insert(uuid.to_string(), data);\n            }\n            Err(..) \u003d\u003e {}\n        }\n    }\n\n    service_data\n}\n```\n\nAnd then implement iterator for adv data:\n```\nstruct AdvDataIterator\u003c\u0027a\u003e {\n    data: \u0026\u0027a[u8],\n    data_type: u8,\n    cur: usize, // to keep current position\n    ...\n}\n\nimpl\u003c\u0027a\u003e Iterator for AdvDataIterator\u003c\u0027a\u003e {\n    type Item \u003d \u0026\u0027a[u8];\n    fn next(\u0026mut self) -\u003e Option\u003c\u0026\u0027a[u8]\u003e {\n        // implement to get the next slice maintaining current position.\n    }\n}\n\nfn iterate_adv_data(data: \u0026[u8], data_type: u8) -\u003e AdvDataIterator {\n    AdvDataIterator { data, data_type, cur: 0 }\n}\n\n```",
